# Owner correction — package-owned automatic consultation

The owner corrects the final authority's host-dependency split.

There is no orchestrator dependency for Navigator-assisted use. The package can and must provide its own narrowly fixed automatic-consultation surface, following the Recorder precedent: the caller selects one existing package role invocation; a package-owned Assisted Runner observes and honestly settles that invocation, captures the fresh Navigator evidence, automatically invokes/seals Navigator, and returns control. Navigator itself never calls roles. The Runner never chooses the current or next role, route, ordering, repetition, budget, stopping, worktree policy, merge policy, or whether the caller follows advice.

Recorder remains a one-native-invocation sealer and must not be broadened into a composer. Assisted Runner is a distinct package-owned layer above Recorder and Navigator. It may reuse package-owned contracts/components but must preserve Recorder's public contract and one-invocation truth.

Within Navigator-assisted parent-issue mode, automatic consultation is a package-delivered guarantee, not a separately implemented orchestrator feature. External callers remain free not to enter this mode and remain free to disregard ordinary advice. The package may require caller-supplied typed acquisition inputs where the package cannot lawfully infer facts, but must not require a separate workflow-orchestrator product to obtain the automatic role-settlement-to-Navigator lifecycle.

Finalize the smallest honest V1 that delivers this guarantee for the package's own roles. Do not reopen the settled Navigator profession or turn the Runner into a scheduler.